\ Give each of K cutlets a distinct name from the canonical 17 names.
\ Names use canonical indices 1..17 and their index is the displayed
\ cutlet value. The cutlet's ORDINAL position is a different number.
\ The first sequence in dictionary order is 1,2,...,K.
\ The final sequence for K=3 is 17,16,15.
\ There are 17!/(17-K)! possible sequences without repeated names.
\ Bowl 5 and seal 22 choose one exact sequence from the shared year sauce.
\ This source has not been compiled or executed by CAL.

A cutlet name assignment is a thing with
  a number called name index.

The chosen cutlet names are some cutlet name assignments.
The new cutlet name assignment is a cutlet name assignment.
The examined cutlet name assignment is a cutlet name assignment.

A cutlet name choice has
  a number called names chosen,
  a number called candidate index,
  a number called used status,
  a number called selection success,
  a number called available names,
  a number called names still required,
  a wide quantity called total sequences,
  a wide quantity called tail sequences,
  a wide quantity called remaining rank.

The cutlet name choice is a cutlet name choice.
The requested cutlet name index is a number.

\ Compute a falling factorial, not a power of seventeen.
To count all cutlet name sequences:
  Put "1" into the cutlet name choice's total sequences.
  Put 17 into the cutlet name choice's available names.
  Put the selected cutlet count into the cutlet name choice's names still required.
  Loop.
    If the cutlet name choice's names still required is 0, break.
    Multiply the cutlet name choice's total sequences by the cutlet name choice's available names.
    Subtract 1 from the cutlet name choice's available names.
    Subtract 1 from the cutlet name choice's names still required.
  Repeat.

\ Once one more name has been fixed, the number of complete suffixes
\ is P(17-chosen-1, K-chosen-1), independent of the candidate identity.
To count cutlet name suffixes:
  Put "1" into the cutlet name choice's tail sequences.
  Put 17 into the cutlet name choice's available names.
  Subtract the cutlet name choice's names chosen from the cutlet name choice's available names.
  Subtract 1 from the cutlet name choice's available names.
  Put the selected cutlet count into the cutlet name choice's names still required.
  Subtract the cutlet name choice's names chosen from the cutlet name choice's names still required.
  Subtract 1 from the cutlet name choice's names still required.
  Loop.
    If the cutlet name choice's names still required is 0, break.
    Multiply the cutlet name choice's tail sequences by the cutlet name choice's available names.
    Subtract 1 from the cutlet name choice's available names.
    Subtract 1 from the cutlet name choice's names still required.
  Repeat.

\ Each candidate is inspected against the names already committed.
To inspect the candidate cutlet name:
  Put 0 into the cutlet name choice's used status.
  Put the chosen cutlet names' first into the examined cutlet name assignment.
  Loop.
    If the examined cutlet name assignment is nil, break.
    If the examined cutlet name assignment's name index is the cutlet name choice's candidate index,
      put 1 into the cutlet name choice's used status; break.
    Put the examined cutlet name assignment's next into the examined cutlet name assignment.
  Repeat.

To remember the new cutlet name:
  Allocate memory for the new cutlet name assignment.
  Put the cutlet name choice's candidate index into the new cutlet name assignment's name index.
  Append the new cutlet name assignment to the chosen cutlet names.
  Add 1 to the cutlet name choice's names chosen.

\ Unranking skips an entire lexicographic block for every unused name
\ that comes before the name at the requested one-based position.
To select the next cutlet name:
  Count cutlet name suffixes.
  Put 1 into the cutlet name choice's candidate index.
  Loop.
    If the cutlet name choice's candidate index is greater than 17, break.
    Inspect the candidate cutlet name.
    If the cutlet name choice's used status is 1,
      add 1 to the cutlet name choice's candidate index; repeat.
    If the cutlet name choice's tail sequences is numerically smaller than the cutlet name choice's remaining rank,
      subtract the cutlet name choice's tail sequences from the cutlet name choice's remaining rank;
      add 1 to the cutlet name choice's candidate index;
      repeat.
    Remember the new cutlet name.
    Break.
  Repeat.

To select cutlet names from a wide quantity:
  Put 0 into the cutlet name choice's selection success.
  Destroy the chosen cutlet names.
  If the selected cutlet count is less than 1, exit.
  If the selected cutlet count is greater than 17, exit.
  If the wide quantity is "0", exit.
  Count all cutlet name sequences.
  If the cutlet name choice's total sequences is numerically smaller than the wide quantity, exit.
  Put the wide quantity into the cutlet name choice's remaining rank.
  Put 0 into the cutlet name choice's names chosen.
  Loop.
    If the cutlet name choice's names chosen is the selected cutlet count, break.
    Select the next cutlet name.
    If the cutlet name choice's candidate index is greater than 17, exit.
  Repeat.
  Put 1 into the cutlet name choice's selection success.

\ Rebuild the SAME structure sauce if a gate walk has overwritten bowls.
\ Do not choose again the cutlet partition or cutlet count.
To choose the canonical cutlet names:
  Prepare the year structure sauce.
  Count all cutlet name sequences.
  Put 5 into the seal inquiry's bowl identity.
  Put 22 into the seal inquiry's seal number.
  Begin a sealed inquiry.
  Choose an equal option given the cutlet name choice's total sequences.
  Select cutlet names from the seal inquiry's selected quantity.

\ Convert a cutlet ordinal position (1..K) into its canonical name.
To read the requested cutlet name:
  Put 0 into the requested cutlet name index.
  Put 1 into a name ordinal number.
  Put the chosen cutlet names' first into the examined cutlet name assignment.
  Loop.
    If the examined cutlet name assignment is nil, break.
    If the name ordinal number is the requested cutlet number,
      put the examined cutlet name assignment's name index into the requested cutlet name index; break.
    Put the examined cutlet name assignment's next into the examined cutlet name assignment.
    Add 1 to the name ordinal number.
  Repeat.
